# Tang

- Prefer deterministic checks (`make verify`, linters, tests) over prose rules or comments.
- Spend most of the turn on verification evidence after code changes.
- When you correct the same agent mistake twice, encode it as a lint/CI check (use `tang-harden`).
- Do not add drive-by markdown, comments, or refactors unrelated to the task.
- Before claiming done: run `make verify` (or `tang verify`) and report the output.
